      "@type": "NewsArticle",
      "headline": "Vishwashanti Gurukul World School Hosts Dr. Kiran Bedi as Chief Guest for Annual Day 2024",
      "articleBody": "Vishwashanti Gurukul World School, Pune celebrated its Annual Day 2024 with a display of talent, culture, and creativity, featuring Dr. Kiran Bedi as the chief guest. The programme commenced with a Welcome Address by Vice Principal Mr. Arpit Sharma, followed by the World Peace Prayer, the Lighting of the Lamp, and the Ganesh Vandana.\n\nThe Curtain Raiser, titled 'So Many Colours', was performed by EY1 and EY2 students. The Australian Chair Dance, Academic Toppers Reward, and Sports Achievement segment followed. Dr. Kiran Bedi addressed students on perseverance and the importance of education in shaping futures.\n\nPYP 1 students performed a Hawaiian Dance; PYP 2 performed John Lennon's 'Imagine'. Cultural performances included an Indian Classical Group Song, a Tribute to Raj Kapoor (honouring the ideals of the school's founder, Professor Dr. Vishwanath Karad), a Maori Haka Dance, an Afro Jazz Dance, a drama on non-violence and peace, Russian and French Dance, and Japanese Dance.\n\nThe Annual School Report was presented by Head Boy Rohan George and Head Girl Shreya. Musical performances included a Drum Circle, Guitar, 'We Are the World', and a Fusion & Culmination performance. The event concluded with a Vote of Thanks by PYP Coordinator Ms. Dimpal Juneja and the National Anthem.\n\nAbout Chief Guest Dr. Kiran Bedi: Dr. Kiran Bedi is a distinguished leader known for her pioneering work in public service as India's first female Indian Police Service (IPS) officer, a celebrated author and motivational speaker.",
